{title: Red River Valley}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 96}
{meta: public_domain Traditional North American song; an early version was published in 1896 as "In the Bright Mohawk Valley".}
{meta: arrangement Original chord arrangement for Fretlight}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
From this [G]valley they say you are [G]going,
We will [G]miss your bright eyes and sweet [D]smile,
For they [G]say you are taking the [G7]sunshine
That [C]brightens our [D]pathway a[G]while.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Come and [G]sit by my side if you [G]love me,
Do not [G]hasten to bid me a[D]dieu,
But re[G]member the Red River [G7]Valley,
And the [C]one who has [D]loved you so [G]true.
{end_of_chorus}
